@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-10
@reviewed: 2026-10-15
@allow-many-consumes: "Script composer: each consumed fragment renders one section of the generated script."

Feature: Site Provisioning Script Generator
  "Renders the idempotent script that stands up a site on its server (apex domain or subdomain): a mason-owned, group-readable web root, Caddy group access, and a Mason-managed static vhost named by the site's host. Apex domains also get a www→apex redirect."

  Provides:
    - setup.ProvisionParams @source("symbol:ProvisionParams")
    - setup.ProvisionScript @source("symbol:ProvisionScript")
    - setup.SnippetPath @source("symbol:SnippetPath")

  Consumes:
    - config.Site
    - setup.writeScriptPreamble
    - setup.writeCaddyGroupAccessBlock
    - setup.writeSnippetInstall
    - setup.writeCaddyImportBlock
    - setup.writeCaddyReloadBlock

  Invariants:
    - ProvisionScript MUST be a deterministic, pure function of its params
    - The snippet file MUST be named by the site's URL host (<snippet dir>/<host>.caddy), never by a user-chosen name, so two projects cannot overwrite each other's vhost
    - The snippet MUST start with the managed marker; an existing snippet without it MUST NOT be replaced unless forced
    - The vhost MUST be a static file_server and MUST 404 every dotfile path except /.well-known/*, after any SPA try_files and before file_server
    - The vhost MUST NOT include the share store's /objects/* private-prefix matcher
    - Apex vs subdomain MUST be auto-detected via the Public Suffix List, overridable by DomainMode; an apex MUST be served from the bare apex and (unless NoWWW) get a permanent www→apex redirect; a www-prefixed URL MUST normalize to the same result
    - SPA MUST add try_files {path} /index.html; it comes from the site config or the --spa flag
    - The script MUST NOT create users, groups, SSH keys, or share scaffolding
    - The web root MUST be 2750, mason-owned, group-readable so Caddy can serve it
    - A reload MUST be gated by caddy validate with rollback; without Reload the script only prints the manual steps

  OutOfScope:
    - Server bootstrap: users, keys, the Caddyfile import discipline (setup.BootstrapScript)
    - Share store provisioning (setup.ShareStoreScript)
    - Running the script over SSH (cli provision)
    - Deploying content (deploy)

  Scenario (happy-path): Subdomain site
    Given a site https://blog.example.com
    When ProvisionScript renders
    Then it creates the web root, writes mason.d/blog.example.com.caddy with the marker and dotfile 404, and imports it once

  Scenario (happy-path): Apex domain with www redirect
    Given a site https://example.com or https://www.example.com
    When ProvisionScript renders
    Then it serves the bare apex and adds a permanent www.example.com → apex redirect block

  Scenario (negative): Hand-written snippet
    Given an existing snippet without the managed marker and FORCE unset
    When the script runs
    Then it prints the diff, leaves the file alone, and exits 3

  Scenario (edge): SPA fallback
    Given SPA is true
    When ProvisionScript renders
    Then the vhost has try_files {path} /index.html before the dotfile matcher and file_server
